cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "AlgoGens Library: a dataset of systems where generative models propose and algorithms judge"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ashachar/algogens-library-data"
url: "https://algogens.org/library/"
authors:
  - family-names: Shachar
    given-names: Amir
    affiliation: Riskernel
    email: amir@riskernel.com
keywords:
  - AlgoGens
  - generative AI
  - algorithms
  - program search
  - automated theorem proving
  - verifier-guided generation
  - agent harness
abstract: >-
  The AlgoGens Library lists published systems in which a generative model proposes
  candidates, an algorithm or another authority (a proof assistant, a verifier, a simulator,
  an evaluator) judges them, and the judgment steers the next proposals. Each card records
  the loop, the headline result as stated in its primary source, what the result does not
  prove, a classification along fixed fields, and the sources checked. The dataset also
  lists installable open-source tools built on the same pattern.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Introduction to Algogens: Integrating Generative AI with Algorithmic Frameworks"
    authors:
